{"title":"2012 OIM Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_OIM_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Equilateral triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/b/98b343102656e4215fb193c395c2a287b46ac99d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/1/39191b218350a52050b4d6161b4c5c67e042bc9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DCY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> are drawn on a rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> so that each one shares points with the interior of the rectangle. Line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d857b2c804701b561a5c8c90c400f360d27232c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX$\" width=\"29\" height=\"13\" /> cuts line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/a/03a548f8f2bc6dfce44eed33b1da3c8afd1b118f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AY$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> cuts line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />. Prove that the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/0/880518fa90ebed1440cedcc1a86d052a01c4b434.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$APQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> is equilateral.\n</p><p>~translated into English by Tomas Diaz. ~orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_OIM_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>This problem needs a solution. If you have a solution for it, please help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2012_OIM_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit\">adding it</a></span>.</i> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_OIM_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=OIM_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"OIM Problems and Solutions\">OIM Problems and Solutions</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017033517\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.014 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 66/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 423/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser f